## Metadata
Title: FUN's Cross-Word Puzzle
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1914-02-15
Number: 9
Description: A 13-wide diamond with a shaded cross in the centre carrying the printed number (shown as _), and two words printed in the grid as a starter: FUN (r2c6-c8) and PUZZLES (r4c4-c10); clues name four words by those printed letters (F-4, P-23, N-5, S-24).
Source: Milwaukee Sentinel, 1914-02-15, p. 83
Solution-Source: Milwaukee Sentinel, 1914-02-22, p. 83


## Printed
heading: FUN'S CROSS-WORD PUZZLES
subheading: SOLVE THEM IF YOU CAN.
intro: Today's cross-word puzzle, the ninth in FUN'S series, will be found somewhat easier than the one given last week. You have two words already provided as a starter—FUN and PUZZLES.
instructions: Fill in the small squares in the diamond with words corresponding to the clews and definitions given herewith, allowing one letter of the word to each small square.
intro: On another page you will find the solution to last week's cross-word puzzle, showing just how the letters are to be placed to form words reading across and up and down.
intro: The solution to today's puzzle will be given in next week's FUN.
number: No 9
solution heading: SOLUTION TO No. 9 PUZZLE
solution caption: Here is the solution to the ninth in FUN'S series, cross-word puzzles, showing the cross-words that fit the list of clews and definitions given. See if you can solve today's cross-word puzzle.


